{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":852,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Moreover Elihu answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2719},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":853,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Do you think this to be your right, or do you say, ‘My righteousness is more than God’s,’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2721},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":854,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"that you ask, ‘What advantage will it be to you? What profit will I have, more than if I had sinned?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2724},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":855,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"I will answer you, and your companions with you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2727},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":856,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Look to the skies, and see. See the skies, which are higher than you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2730},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":857,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"If you have sinned, what effect do you have against him? If your transgressions are multiplied, what do you do to him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2733},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":858,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"If you are righteous, what do you give him? Or what does he receive from your hand?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2736},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":859,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Your wickedness may hurt a man as you are, and your righteousness may profit a son of man.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2739},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":860,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"“By reason of the multitude of oppressions they cry out. They cry for help by reason of the arm of the mighty.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2743},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":861,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"But no one says, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives songs in the night,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2746},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":862,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"who teaches us more than the animals of the earth, and makes us wiser than the birds of the sky?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2749},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":863,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"There they cry, but no one answers, because of the pride of evil men.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2752},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":864,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"Surely God will not hear an empty cry, neither will the Almighty regard it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2755},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":865,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"How much less when you say you don’t see him. The cause is before him, and you wait for him!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2758},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":866,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"But now, because he has not visited in his anger, neither does he greatly regard arrogance,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2761},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":35,"verse_ordinal":867,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"therefore Job opens his mouth with empty talk, and he multiplies words without knowledge.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2764}]}